Package: inphDrugRepurposing
Title: Computational Drug Repurposing for iNPH via Interferon-Activated
    Monocyte Signature Reversal
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Masudul", "Haque", email = "masud.biochem.cu@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computational pipeline reanalyzing a public single-cell RNA-seq
    atlas of idiopathic normal pressure hydrocephalus (iNPH) to identify a
    type I interferon-activated classical monocyte subcluster, derive a
    300-gene cell-state signature, contextualize its magnitude against
    systemic lupus erythematosus, and screen it against the LINCS L1000
    perturbation database (THP1-primary connectivity ranking) to nominate
    drug repurposing candidates. Includes an orthogonal Hallmark
    interferon-alpha gene-set sensitivity analysis. Supports the analysis
    reported in the associated manuscript, submitted to npj Systems Biology
    and Applications.
